raylib for generated9

Install libgpu and libtinygl first (boot/GPU.md), then build:

    cd /sys/src/libraylib
    mk install
    cd examples
    mk install
    games/raydemo

The native backend uses rio, TinyGL/VirGL and /dev/audio. Clients compile
with -p; headers select the libraries. See raylib(2) for API conventions,
window and audio behavior, and classic GL limits.

raydemo shows a textured cube and a second camera rendered into a texture.
Space pauses, arrows orbit and the wheel zooms. -a adds sound; -n limits frames.

Tests, inside a rio window with VirGL available:

    cd /sys/src/libraylib/test
    mk test
    ./6.out -a

The optional -a run needs /dev/audio. Tests cover rendering, render textures,
images, models/animation, files, input, clocks and resource lifetime; audio
tests cover decoding, resampling, streaming and playback state.
Runtime validation used amd64/QEMU VirGL and HDA. Other architectures
have not been tested. External test assets are not installed or bundled.

See UPSTREAM and LICENSE for imported sources, adaptations and notices.
